Aim: 
To perform calculations using aggregate functions and group records based on conditions.

Algorithm:
1. Use the employee table.
2. Apply aggregate functions.
3. Group records by department.
4. Filter groups using HAVING.
5. Display the results.

Program:
-- Count employees
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM EMPLOYEE;

-- Find total salary
SELECT SUM(SALARY) FROM EMPLOYEE;

-- Find average salary
SELECT AVG(SALARY) FROM EMPLOYEE;

-- Find maximum salary
SELECT MAX(SALARY) FROM EMPLOYEE;

-- Find minimum salary
SELECT MIN(SALARY) FROM EMPLOYEE;

-- Group employees by department
SELECT DEPARTMENT, COUNT(*)
FROM EMPLOYEE
GROUP BY DEPARTMENT;

-- Departments having average salary above 28000
SELECT DEPARTMENT, AVG(SALARY)
FROM EMPLOYEE
GROUP BY DEPARTMENT
HAVING AVG(SALARY) > 28000;

Result:
Aggregate functions and grouping conditions were executed successfully
